  "kind": "synth",
  "contract": "exact",
  "idea": "Write p = (-1)^n for photon-number parity. On the verified subspace n in {0,1,2,3}, any function of n is a line on each parity class (two points per class), giving n^2 = 3n - p n + (3/2) p - 3/2 exactly. Hence exp(-i theta n^2) = e^{i 3theta/2} R(3theta) exp(+i theta p n) exp(-i (3theta/2) p); all three diagonal-in-n factors commute. A local qubit coupled to the mode is parity-mapped by V = H . CR(pi) . H = exp(-i pi n X/2) (exact for every n: I, -iX, -I, iX on n = 0,1,2,3), so V|0,n> = c_n |n mod 2, n> with the ancilla's Z eigenvalue equal to p. CR(-2theta) . rz(3theta) then realises exp(-i(3theta/2 - theta n) p) on the mapped register; V^+ unmaps it, the c_n phases cancel against their conjugates, and the ancilla returns exactly to |0> for every n. R(3theta) supplies the remaining 3n term and a dropped global phase completes exp(-i theta n^2). Exact only on n <= 3; beyond that the construction still realises a well-defined but different diagonal unitary.",
  "term_kinds": [
   "n2"
  ],
  "stage": "logical"
 },
